'''Liko's homeroom teacher''' is a minor recurring character in ''[[Pokémon Horizons: The Series]]''. He is one of the teachers at [[Indigo Academy]] and teaches [[Liko]] and [[Ann]].
==In animation==
===History===
[[File:Teacher and Liko.png|250px|thumb|left|Liko's homeroom teacher gifting [[Liko]] with her [[first partner Pokémon]]]]
Before the events of ''[[Pokémon Horizons: The Series]]'', Liko's homeroom teacher was responsible for conducting Liko's interviews before joining Indigo Academy.

[[Liko]]'s homeroom teacher first appeared in a flashback in ''[[HZ001|The Pendant That Starts It All (Part One)]]''. Later, he was responsible for delivering the [[first partner Pokémon]] of students in Liko's class, including her {{TP|Liko|Sprigatito}} and [[Ann]]'s {{p|Oshawott}}.

Liko's homeroom teacher briefly appeared in ''[[HZ008|The Door That Never Opens]]''.

In ''[[HZ035|The Wild Pair, Friede and Cap!]]'', he reappeared teaching a class about Pokémon and bonding with its Trainer. As part of the class, he assigned the class to choose a Trainer and their Pokémon to present in the next class. The next day, he was seen with the class watching Liko's dissertation on [[Friede]] and [[Captain Pikachu]].

In ''[[HZ040|Farewell, Sprigatito?]]'', he reappeared in a flashback to Liko's initial interview, where it was revealed that [[Marnya]] was with the teacher during that interview and noticed enormous potential in the girl.

In ''[[HZ113|Mega Evolution - Ult]]'', he appeared in a flashback while [[Roy]] was telling [[Emma]] about the whereabouts of the remaining [[Rising Volt Tacklers]].

